==Swedish==

===Etymology===
From dialectal {{m|sv|pula||work, toil, pound, hit, have sex, mate, and more}}. Compare {{cog|da|pule}}, {{cog|is|púla}}. Perhaps the same word as {{cog|gml|pulen||extricate with the fingers}}, and cognate with {{cog|ang|pullian||to pluck, pull}}. See also {{m|sv|pulla||finger}}.

===Verb===
{{sv-verb-reg}}

# {{lb|sv|colloquial}} to [[tinker]], to [[potter]]
#: {{syn|sv|påta|pyssla}}
# {{lb|sv|with a particle like {{m|sv|ner||down}} or {{m|sv|in||in}}}} to [[stuff]] (press, compressing or scrunching)
#: {{ux|sv|Han '''pulade ner''' papperslappen i fickan|He '''stuffed''' the piece of paper into his pocket}}
# {{lb|sv|colloquial|regional}} to [[rub]] [[snow]] in someone's [[face]]
#: {{syn|sv|snöpula|mula}}

